From 143f1d878296176c738274202092bb247b7b771c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naster17 <naster17.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:26:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Honor the terminating -1 visibility selector in profiler
 agent filtering

Stop evaluating later GPU agents before the invalid-token CI diagnostic, preserving selections matched earlier in the list. This prevents the supported masking sentinel from aborting Torch import.

Test: isolated one-unit ccache build and retained-input relink on BC250; candidate direct HIP/CUDA/ROCR -1 imports, valid0/terminated selectors and FP64 output/backward plus CPU-first profiler gates in daily and RCCL profiles. UUID unsupported by this board; production SDK unchanged.
---
 .../rocprofiler-sdk/source/lib/rocprofiler-sdk/agent.cpp     | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/projects/rocprofiler-sdk/source/lib/rocprofiler-sdk/agent.cpp b/projects/rocprofiler-sdk/source/lib/rocprofiler-sdk/agent.cpp
index ac56e51f7c..e6adbcae83 100644
--- a/projects/rocprofiler-sdk/source/lib/rocprofiler-sdk/agent.cpp
+++ b/projects/rocprofiler-sdk/source/lib/rocprofiler-sdk/agent.cpp
@@ -196,6 +196,11 @@ update_agent_runtime_visibility(rocprofiler_agent_t& agent_info)
             {
                 if(itr.empty()) continue;
 
+                // A terminating visibility sentinel selects no further GPU agents.
+                // Preserve selections matched earlier in the list; do not escalate
+                // this supported filter value to a fatal CI diagnostic.
+                if(itr == "-1") break;
+
                 ROCP_TRACE << "Processing " << env_varname << " token: " << itr;
 
                 auto _idx_v = idx++;
-- 
2.56.0

